+**Steps:**
+1.  Compute the squared L2 norm for each vector by summing the squares of its components.
+2.  Take the square root of the sum to obtain the L2 norm.
+3.  Divide each component of the original vectors by their respective L2 norm plus a stability constant $\epsilon$ to obtain normalized vectors on the unit hypersphere.
+4.  Compute the dot product of the two normalized vectors.
+5.  Return the dot product as the similarity score.
+
+**Formulas:**
+*   L2 norm: $\|\mathbf{z}\|_2 = \sqrt{\sum_{k=1}^d z_k^2}$ [S1, unofficial].
+*   Normalization map: $\hat{\mathbf{z}} = \phi(\mathbf{z}) = \frac{\mathbf{z}}{\|\mathbf{z}\|_2 + \epsilon}$, where $\phi: \mathbb{R}^d \to S^{d-1}$ maps to the unit hypersphere [S1, unofficial].
+*   Similarity: $sim = \hat{\mathbf{z}}_{\text{render}}^\top \hat{\mathbf{z}}_{\text{target}} = \cos \theta$, where $\theta$ is the angle between the original vectors [S1, unofficial].
 
